(n) the form and the time for preparing annual report under sub-section (2) of section 42;
(o) the compensation for the premature termination of employment under the second proviso to sub-section (3) of section 58; (p) any other matter in respect of which provision is to be made byrules.

55. Power to make regulations.-
(1) The Commission may, by notification, make regulations consistent with this Act and the rules made thereunder to carry out the provisions of this Act.
(2) In particular, and without prejudice to the generality of the foregoing power, such regulations may provide for all or any of the following matters, namely:-
